2026-11-06T13:49:28.8471444Z Run one block of tests/features.py, from a marker line to the next block.
2026-11-06T13:49:28.8472101Z 
2026-11-06T13:49:28.8472646Z     python3 tools/audit/seat/features_block.py [--prelude 'import line']... "<first line of the block>" [END]
2026-11-06T13:49:28.8473769Z     python3 tools/audit/seat/features_block.py [--prelude 'import line']... --through "<marker line>"
2026-11-06T13:49:28.8474329Z 
2026-11-06T13:49:28.8474758Z features.py runs every block in one process, which takes tens of minutes on a
2026-11-06T13:49:28.8475636Z loaded seat; a mutation proof needs only the block that pins the mutated line.
2026-11-06T13:49:28.8476491Z The block is the text from the line containing START up to END (default: the
2026-11-06T13:49:28.8477159Z script's closing ``sys.exit``), executed in the namespace features.py's own
2026-11-06T13:49:28.8477791Z header builds -- ``R``, ``Coord``, the harness fakes -- with ``__file__``
2026-11-06T13:49:28.8478415Z pointing at features.py, so path arithmetic inside the block resolves as in
2026-11-06T13:49:28.8479333Z the full run. Exit status is the block's ``R.close``: 0 when every check passed.
2026-11-06T13:49:28.8479885Z Run from the repository root under the CI venv.
2026-11-06T13:49:28.8480126Z 
2026-11-06T13:49:28.8480452Z ``--prelude`` (repeatable) runs one line, typically an import an earlier block
2026-11-06T13:49:28.8481126Z made, before the block. ``--through MARKER`` takes no block: it runs the whole
2026-11-06T13:49:28.8481762Z script from the top up to the line holding MARKER, the state every earlier
2026-11-06T13:49:28.8482309Z block builds, and exits with that prefix's ``R.close``.
2026-11-06T13:49:28.8482574Z 
2026-11-06T13:49:28.8482895Z ``--self-test`` runs offline: it executes a two-check block it writes itself.
